I was able to reproduce this in the webapp part (deleted the input field for version.)
Even with:

```
    public function rules()
    {
        return [
            [['version', ...], 'trim'],
            [['version', ...], 'required'],         
            [['version', ...], 'integer'],
        ];
    }
```

My current workaround is checking if the attribute is sent. Example:

```
public function actionUpdate($id)
{
    $model = $this->findModel($id);
    $model->scenario = 'update';
    $stale = false;

    if (ArrayHelper::keyExists($model->optimisticLock(), Yii::$app->request->post($model->formName(), []))
        && $model->load(Yii::$app->request->post())) {
        try {
            if ($model->save()) {
                return $this->redirect(['view', 'id' => $model->id]);
            }
        } catch (yii\db\StaleObjectException $e) {
            $stale = true;
            Yii::$app->session->setFlash('danger', 'Data outdated');
        }
    }

    return $this->render('update', [
        'model' => $model,
        'isStale' => $stale,
    ]);
}
```

